            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s4["5. **User-provided slug**: If the user explicitly passes a slug (e.g., `slug=offline-mode`, `--slug offline-mode`, or an obvious slug-like token), normalize it: lowercase; convert runs of whitespace/underscores to `-`; keep only lowercase letters `a–z`, digits `0–9`, and `-`; drop every other character (including `.`, `/`, `\`); collapse repeated `-`; strip leading/trailing `-`. Do not append timestamps or numbers."]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s5["6. **Interactive mode** (a human is driving): If no slug was provided, **ask the user** and wait. Suggest a 2–4 word kebab-case candidate derived from the idea as a default."]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s6["7. **Automated / non-interactive mode** (no human to ask): Generate a concise slug yourself (2–4 kebab-case words). The generated slug **MUST** produce a unique directory — if `.specify/assessments/<slug>/` already exists, append the shortest disambiguating suffix (`-2`, `-3`, …) or a short ISO-style date (`-20260715`). Never overwrite an existing assessment directory."]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s7["8. **Refuse outright** (do not fetch, do not prompt). Record the URL and reason in `intake.md`:"]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s8["9. **Fetch without prompting** when the host is a widely-used public source: `github.com`, `gist.github.com`, `gitlab.com`, `bitbucket.org`, `*.atlassian.net`, `linear.app`, `notion.so`, `*.notion.site`, `docs.google.com`, `stackoverflow.com`, `*.stackexchange.com`."]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s9["10. **Otherwise** the host is unrecognized:"]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s10["11. **Capture the idea, redacting secrets.** Preserve the original wording (quoted) plus the source (URL, pasted block, or repo path) — but apply the same sanitization as the Source field *inside the quoted text too*: sanitize any credential-bearing URL and redact tokens, passwords, API keys, or cookies. Never persist a secret just because it appeared in the original."]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s11["12. **Restate it in one or two neutral sentences.** What is being proposed, in plain language, without endorsing or dismissing it."]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s12["13. **Record origin and context.** Who raised it, when, and any triggering event (a complaint, an outage, a sales ask, a strategy shift). Mark unknowns as `[NEEDS CLARIFICATION: …]`."]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s13["14. **Note the idea type** so downstream stages know what to weigh: `new-capability` | `improvement` | `fix` | `exploration` | `cost-saving` | `compliance` | `other`."]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s14["15. **List first-glance unknowns** — the obvious questions that must be answered before anyone decides. Do not answer them here."]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s15["16. **Write the intake note** to `ASSESS_DIR/intake.md`:"]
            flow:governance:speckit_assess_intake:execution_workflow_s16["17. **Report back** with:"]
